iperf3 servers listening on ports 5201, 5202, 5203, 5204, 5205, 5206
guests reachable with iperf3: V1=tenant1, V2=tenant5, A=tenant2, B=tenant3, C=tenant4, D=tenant6
SCENARIO steady4: flooder A (tenant2) t=0-28 s (2 streams), flooder B (tenant3) t=6-34 s (2 streams), flooder C (tenant4) t=12-40 s (2 streams), flooder D (tenant6) t=18-40 s (2 streams), all active 18-28 s (Jain window), no bursts
CONFIGS: static 2500 (Mbit/s per flooder, 10 Gbit/s total), static 3500 (Mbit/s per flooder, 14 Gbit/s total), lqr 79_4, lqr 85_4, lqr 90_4, vfrot 0.8_1_2_0.94 (thresh 0.94)
TOKEN BUCKET: all modes use the same xdp_limit.o on every flooder interface, burst 5 ms at the cap rate; victim interfaces never limited (counter only)
VICTIMS: V1 = tenant1 10.10.0.11 port 5201, V2 = tenant5 10.10.0.15 port 5205, each 9 Gbit/s, one stream, constant for [0,40) s (launched together 0.5 s after the flooders); slo_ok per victim = fraction of its 39 1 s windows >= 95% of its own per-repeat reference; slo_ok_worst = the smaller of the two
VICTIM CMD V1: ssh alpine@10.10.0.11 'iperf3 -c 10.10.0.1 -p 5201 -t 40 -b 9G -J'
VICTIM CMD V2: ssh alpine@10.10.0.15 'iperf3 -c 10.10.0.1 -p 5205 -t 40 -b 9G -J'
FLOODER CMD A: ssh alpine@10.10.0.12 'iperf3 -c 10.10.0.1 -p 5202 -t 28 -P 2 -J'
FLOODER CMD B: ssh alpine@10.10.0.13 'sleep 6; iperf3 -c 10.10.0.1 -p 5203 -t 28 -P 2 -J'
FLOODER CMD C: ssh alpine@10.10.0.14 'sleep 12; iperf3 -c 10.10.0.1 -p 5204 -t 28 -P 2 -J'
FLOODER CMD D: ssh alpine@10.10.0.16 'sleep 18; iperf3 -c 10.10.0.1 -p 5206 -t 22 -P 2 -J'
REF CMD V1: ssh alpine@10.10.0.11 'iperf3 -c 10.10.0.1 -p 5201 -t 10 -b 9G -J' (both together, 2 runs)
REF CMD V2: ssh alpine@10.10.0.15 'iperf3 -c 10.10.0.1 -p 5205 -t 10 -b 9G -J' (both together, 2 runs)
vfrot: feedback = WORST victim, min over V1/V2 of EMA(1 s rate)/own reference < thresh; budget start 10000, clamp [800, 16000] Mbit/s, rotation over 4 holders (holder gets B - (n_active - 1) x 200); static/lqr never see the victims
vfrot NOTE: budget start 10000 and ceiling 16000 Mbit/s kept from exp38 (4 vCPU) for comparability; with more CPU room on 6 vCPU the 16000 Mbit/s ceiling could become binding (check budget_mbit in the ts file)
